<title>JAPAN: Matsushita says no plan to invest in BSkyB itself.</title>
<headline>Matsushita says no plan to invest in BSkyB itself.</headline>
<dateline>OSAKA, Japan 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Matsushita Electric Industrial Co Ltd said on Wednesday that it is not considering investing in British Sky Broadcasting Group Plc (BSkyB) itself, although it plans to form a joint venture with the company.</p>
<p>Asked whether the Japanese consumer electronics giant has any plans to invest in BSkyB itself, Mikio Higashi, a Matsushita director, told a news conference: &quot;We have no such ideas.&quot;</p>
<p>Earlier, Matsushita announced it would take part in a new joint venture, worth 265 million pounds, with BSkyB and two other firms to deliver digital interactive services in Britain.</p>
<p>Matsushita will take a 15 percent stake in the venture.</p>
